{
  "cell": "bias_core_settle_flag",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md",
    "for the recipe this follows and layout/bias_core_settle_flag/README.md",
    "for this cell's own floorplan/routing reasoning and results. Issue #39",
    "(part of #34, itself a follow-on from #30/#4); the compose-cell recipe",
    "is the one layout/bias_core_pnp8_leg/ (issue #30/PR #33) established.",
    "",
    "This is design/netlist/bias_core.spice's XMPOK/XMOKA/XMOKB/XMOL1/XMOL2/",
    "XMOKC/XMOK2/XMOK2P/XMO1P/XMO1N device group -- the settle-flag",
    "comparator/driver chain that produces bias_core's own BIAS_OK output.",
    "10 devices, 5x sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 + 5x",
    "sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5, each its own single-instance `klt gen",
    "mos_array` call (rows=1 cols=1 dummy=0 gate_contact=true) -- no matched",
    "array: no two of these ten devices share a W/L, and none of them are",
    "meant to match each other.",
    "",
    "KNOWN GAP, disclosed here because a clean LVS match below cannot see",
    "it: `klt gen` cannot draw sky130's hvi (75/20) thick-oxide marker, so",
    "these are the 5V devices' W/L drawn in the 1.8V domain's geometry. See",
    "README.md's 'The one thing this layout does not yet say' section and",
    "2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1912.",
    "",
    "FLOORPLAN (placement.strategy 'explicit'): the standard two-row CMOS",
    "shape -- NMOS row along y=0 (orientation 'none', gates facing north),",
    "PMOS row with its bottom edge at y=14.0 (orientation 'mirror_y', or",
    "'rotate_180' for moka whose source must face east, so every PMOS gate",
    "faces south), and the signal channel between them. Every PMOS gate",
    "lands on the same y=14.36 gate row because each PMOS origin is set from",
    "its own device height (Y = 14.0 + w + 0.82 + 0.15). Bodies are tied by",
    "abutment, not by enclosure (a device nested inside a ring is unroutable",
    "-- 2AMLogic/klayout-tools#1493): each PMOS gets its own `guard_ring`",
    "nwell tap island placed so the two nwells OVERLAP by 0.10um (one",
    "electrical node) while their li1 stays 0.20um apart, clear of sky130's",
    "0.17um li1 spacing floor. Distinct nwell islands are kept >= 1.27um",
    "apart (nwell.space.1). moka's tap island sits NORTH of it rather than",
    "west, because a west island would sit exactly where noko's own li1 drop",
    "out of moka's west-facing drain has to run. Two psub tap islands",
    "(add_well=false) tie the substrate to vss.",
    "",
    "ROUTING (three planes, assigned per net via connectivity[].layer_role,",
    "klayout-tools#1655, so no two nets sharing a plane ever cross):",
    "  metal  (li1)  nokl / noko / nokx / bias_ok -- the four local nets,",
    "                each confined to its own column of the channel, in",
    "                disjoint x ranges, so they cannot meet;",
    "  metal2 (met1) vdd (one lane above the PMOS row, y=26.5) and vss (one",
    "                lane below the NMOS row, y=-6.0) -- disjoint by",
    "                construction;",
    "  metal3 (met2) tok (stays above the PMOS row, y>=15.47) and pb (stays",
    "                below it, y<=14.36) -- also disjoint.",
    "Every leg is steered explicitly through connectivity[].legs[]",
    "(klayout-tools#1529) rather than left to the nearest-first spanning",
    "tree, so a rail leg cannot wander across another net's via landing pad;",
    "compose.response.json records routed: true for every named leg.",
    "",
    "na / nbtop / nkg touch exactly one port in this device group, so each",
    "is a pins[] declare-only top-level pin (a label on the gate pad's own",
    "already-drawn li1, no metal routed) rather than a connectivity[] net."
  ],
